# Definite polynomial integrals with real nonzero coefficient denominators.
# The same strategy retains polynomial identities and every denominator condition.

integral(fn(x R) R {(x+1)^2/2},0,1)=7/6

forall c R*:
    integral(fn(x R) R {(x+1)^2/c},0,1)=7/(3*c)

integral(fn(x R) R {(x/2+1)^2},0,2)=14/3

forall c R*:
    integral(fn(x R) R {(x/c+1)^2},0,1)=1/(3*c^2)+1/c+1
